The native YOLOX Burn model implementation in src/models/yolox was initially adapted from
tracel-ai/models/yolox-burn at revision ec1b9e42e6692ef2b95f85c4ba783e07cd3d19af.
That project is distributed under the MIT OR Apache-2.0 licenses; this derivative uses the
Apache-2.0 option (LICENSE-APACHE).

The YOLOX architecture and COCO pretrained model originate from Megvii's YOLOX project:
https://github.com/Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX
The original implementation and pretrained weights are distributed under Apache-2.0.
The development-only tools/export_yolox_fixtures.py assembles a conversion-time reference from a
plain checkout of that repository (Apache-2.0) to generate golden parity fixtures; nothing from it
is bundled or executed at runtime.

The YOLOX letterbox preprocessing in src/data/letterbox.rs resizes with the fast_image_resize
crate (https://github.com/cykooz/fast_image_resize), distributed under the MIT OR Apache-2.0
licenses; this derivative uses the Apache-2.0 option (LICENSE-APACHE).

The experimental src/models/yolov3_tiny, src/models/yolov10, src/models/yolo11, src/models/yolo12,
src/models/yolov8, and src/models/yolo26 implementations interoperate with the public
YOLOv3-Tiny-Ultralytics, YOLOv10 (n/s/m/b/l/x), YOLO11 (n/s/m/l/x, plus the -seg COCO
instance-segmentation and -cls ImageNet-1k classification variants), YOLO12 (n/s/m/l/x), YOLOv8
(n/s/m/l/x, plus the -seg COCO instance-segmentation and -cls ImageNet-1k classification
variants), and YOLO26 (n/s/m/l/x, plus the -seg COCO instance-segmentation and -cls ImageNet-1k
classification variants) architectures and official checkpoints. They were authored as native Burn
code; boquilens does not bundle Ultralytics Python code or model weights.
tools/export_ultralytics_state.py and the per-model export_*_fixtures.py scripts use an installed
Ultralytics package at conversion time to extract tensor state from a checkpoint.
Ultralytics states that its software, architectures, and trained model weights are offered under
AGPL-3.0 by default, with separate commercial licensing available:
https://www.ultralytics.com/license
Because boquilens is AGPL-3.0, checkpoints and the derived native artifacts may be redistributed
under the same license. Users supplying or publishing an Ultralytics checkpoint remain responsible
for satisfying the license applicable to that model and their use case.

