The native training augmentation modules in src/data/augmentation are modified Rust adaptations
of the Ultralytics data augmentation pipeline at commit
461196cf09175b64c9b9bd8babebf081c0540520 (version v8.4.117-2-g461196cf0):
https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics
Ultralytics is distributed under AGPL-3.0. The adapted implementation is modified for native Rust
data containers, deterministic worker-independent random streams, and record/replay diagnostics.
Ultralytics does not endorse boquilens.

The development-only tools/onnx exporter reconstructs Ultralytics-family graphs from the pinned
sibling Ultralytics checkout at revision 461196cf09175b64c9b9bd8babebf081c0540520 and reconstructs
YOLOX graphs from an explicit official 0.1.1rc0 checkout. Those sources are used only while
producing and validating an ONNX artifact and are not bundled into the Rust runtime. Exported
artifacts retain the architecture and checkpoint license/provenance recorded in their embedded
metadata and JSON sidecar: Ultralytics-family artifacts are AGPL-3.0 by default (or the separately
licensed terms applicable to the supplied model), while official YOLOX artifacts retain
Apache-2.0 provenance. ONNX export does not relicense user datasets or checkpoints.

The development-only training fixture exporters run the same pinned Ultralytics source and the
official YOLOX 0.1.1rc0 source to record loss/gradient/optimizer parity evidence. Generated fixtures
are not distributed with boquilens; Ultralytics-derived fixtures inherit AGPL-3.0 and official
YOLOX-derived fixtures retain Apache-2.0 provenance.

The classification RandAugment policy structure and RandomErasing/RandomResizedCrop behavior are
adapted from torchvision, distributed under the BSD 3-Clause License. The applicable license text
is included in LICENSE-TORCHVISION. PyTorch and torchvision do not endorse boquilens.
